# Modem image (item walleye-modem-mss-image): on top of walleye.config, the modem subsystem's remoteproc driver and the rmtfs memory driver built in (the ramdisk carries no modules; defconfig has both =m).
# QCOM_Q6V5_MSS depends on QCOM_SMEM (hard) and on RPMSG_QCOM_SMD, QCOM_SYSMON, RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK_SMEM, RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK and QCOM_AOSS_QMP each `|| =n` (tests/fixtures/kernel-text/modem-mss-Kconfig.txt): SMEM, SMD, GLINK and AOSS_QMP are =y by defconfig, SYSMON and GLINK_SMEM by walleye.config,
# so =y here keeps it =y. QRTR, QRTR_SMD and QCOM_PD_MAPPER (the kernel's own pd-mapper, in since v6.16, present in v7.3) are walleye.config's.
CONFIG_QCOM_Q6V5_MSS=y
CONFIG_QCOM_RMTFS_MEM=y
